=== Bugs found and fixed this session ===
1. navio2-gps-lock.sh: No DRY_RUN early-exit when GPS_STATUS_PATH is missing.
   Unlike navio2-time-sync.sh which exits early when timedatectl is unavailable,
   GPS lock would poll for the full timeout (180s) before the DRY_RUN fallback triggered.
   Fix: Added early-exit check before the polling loop:
     if [ ! -r "$GPS_STATUS_PATH" ] && [ "$DRY_RUN" = "1" ]; then
         warn "GPS status path not readable in dry-run ..."; return 0
     fi

2. navio2-gates.env: All non-DRY_RUN variables used unconditional assignment.
   Same pattern as the DRY_RUN bug fixed in Day 1 — env-var overrides from
   the caller were clobbered by the env file source.
   Fix: Changed all assignments to use ${VAR:-default} pattern.
   Affected: RCIO_ROOT, RCIO_ADC_DIR, PWMCHIP_PATH, SPI_NODE, GPS_STATUS_PATH,
   REQUIRED_MODULES, MODULE_EXPECTED_PATHS, PERMISSIONS_GROUP, PERMISSIONS_MODE,
   PERMISSIONS_PATHS, TIME_SYNC_TIMEOUT_SEC, TIME_SYNC_INTERVAL_SEC,
   GPS_LOCK_VALUE, GPS_TIMEOUT_SEC, GPS_INTERVAL_SEC, ADC_CHANNELS,
   ADC_PATH_PREFIX, PREFLIGHT_LOG_FILE, PREFLIGHT_REQUIRE_SPI,
   RUN_GATES_CONTINUE_ON_FAIL
